WEBVTT

00:34.760 --> 00:37.800
Love, I've got to feel it

00:38.050 --> 00:41.140
If you put your trust in me

00:41.390 --> 00:44.640
I know what my life would be

00:44.770 --> 00:49.520
Oh, you are all I ever need

00:49.690 --> 00:55.240
I try to hear what you say

00:55.360 --> 00:57.490
So I pray

00:57.570 --> 01:01.080
But you're fading away

01:02.540 --> 01:08.250
Don't go and break my fragile heart

01:08.670 --> 01:11.880
We won't fall apart

01:12.010 --> 01:20.050
'Cause you're my only star

01:22.020 --> 01:25.770
I wonder why my tears come at night

01:25.770 --> 01:29.270
Calling you, so like a little child

01:29.440 --> 01:32.530
All the things you have in mind

01:32.780 --> 01:35.900
I wish I could see your insides

01:35.900 --> 01:38.910
My love, you've got to feel it

01:38.910 --> 01:42.240
And if we put our trust in you and me

01:42.450 --> 01:45.870
You know what our lives would be

01:46.000 --> 01:53.840
Oh, you are the one, I believe

02:04.930 --> 02:06.270
Again?

02:06.850 --> 02:08.520
That idiot.

02:17.700 --> 02:19.360
Oh, Himura-kun?

02:20.450 --> 02:21.870
Amamiya-sensei...

02:21.870 --> 02:26.620
What's wrong? Your expression's pretty scary for this early in the morning.

02:26.620 --> 02:31.670
Hmm, taking all of that teenage anger and applying it to art activities instead would truly symbolize youth,

02:31.670 --> 02:33.750
don't you agree?

02:33.750 --> 02:35.880
Meeting you here is a great opportunity.

02:36.420 --> 02:38.630
I don't have any intention of joining the Art Club.

02:38.630 --> 02:40.340
You're no fun.

02:40.340 --> 02:43.930
As for me, I just want to cultivate your talents.

02:43.930 --> 02:45.930
I've told you many times.

02:45.930 --> 02:47.930
I'm not interested in art.

02:48.680 --> 02:50.640
I'm in a hurry, so...

02:50.640 --> 02:52.020
Oh? Nii-san.

02:53.110 --> 02:56.230
What are you doing in a place like this, nii-san?

02:56.230 --> 02:58.740
"Nii-san"? You've started that again?!

02:58.740 --> 03:00.490
Oh, it's Yuko.

03:08.450 --> 03:12.670
I'm in the middle of uncovering a buried river of gold.

03:12.670 --> 03:15.880
Are you referring to Yu-kun as the "river of gold", nii-san?

03:15.880 --> 03:18.380
Amamiya-sensei is your brother?

03:18.380 --> 03:20.380
Didn't I tell you already?

03:20.380 --> 03:22.260
My current name is Amamiya.

03:22.930 --> 03:25.260
Amamiya Yuko, that is.

03:25.810 --> 03:28.640
Amamiya... Yuko?

03:28.640 --> 03:31.230
Ah, you two know each other?

03:31.980 --> 03:36.020
Well, I'm interested in the peculiar relationship between you two,

03:36.020 --> 03:38.530
but I guess we'll have to leave that for next time.

03:38.530 --> 03:40.190
Well then, students.

03:40.190 --> 03:42.490
Study hard.

03:43.860 --> 03:44.700
Well then...

03:44.700 --> 03:47.240
Please study hard,

03:47.240 --> 03:48.870
Mr. Scholarship Student.

03:50.250 --> 03:51.620
Seriously, that's enou—

03:52.460 --> 03:53.830
Hey, Yuko.

03:53.830 --> 03:55.080
What's up?

03:55.080 --> 03:56.840
Where are your slippers?

03:57.630 --> 03:58.750
Who knows?

03:58.750 --> 04:01.720
When I opened my locker this morning, they were gone.

04:01.720 --> 04:02.590
What?

04:02.590 --> 04:04.550
If they're missing, it must be inevitable.

04:04.550 --> 04:05.300
Hey!

04:05.300 --> 04:06.260
Yes?

04:06.260 --> 04:08.890
Go to the faculty room! They'll lend you a pair.

04:09.810 --> 04:10.980
Thanks.

04:10.980 --> 04:13.390
You're kind, Yu-kun.

04:16.900 --> 04:18.570
Wait right here!

04:22.110 --> 04:24.110
let

04:24.110 --> 04:26.030
Here. Put these on.

04:26.030 --> 04:26.820
Oh?

04:26.820 --> 04:28.830
You didn't have to do that for me.

04:29.580 --> 04:33.210
I'd feel guilty if you walked off like that and hurt yourself.

04:33.960 --> 04:35.170
Is that so?

04:35.170 --> 04:36.630
Well, I'm happy.

04:36.630 --> 04:39.090
Thanks so much, Yu-kun.

04:39.090 --> 04:40.590
it

04:40.590 --> 04:41.880
Kuze-san?

04:41.880 --> 04:43.380
Are you at home?

04:45.630 --> 04:47.600
It's Sumire, your next door neighbor.

04:47.600 --> 04:49.760
Are you around, Kuze-san?

04:53.980 --> 04:55.980
Heaven's

04:56.560 --> 04:58.020
Sorry to bother you.

04:58.020 --> 04:59.360
Ah, Himura-kun.

04:59.360 --> 05:01.980
Do you mind if I smoke this to its end?

05:01.980 --> 05:04.320
I just lit it.

05:04.320 --> 05:05.820
I don't mind.

05:05.820 --> 05:08.570
There are no other places where I can smoke freely.

05:09.070 --> 05:11.450
So, what do you want from me?

05:13.620 --> 05:16.420
No matter what you say, I'm not joining the Art Club.

05:16.830 --> 05:18.330
It's about Yuko.

05:18.790 --> 05:22.710
She was at a church orphanage before we adopted her.

05:22.710 --> 05:24.590
Were you there too?

05:24.590 --> 05:25.670
Yes.

05:26.550 --> 05:28.840
I just found it odd that she's so attached to you.

05:28.840 --> 05:31.350
So you two are childhood friends.

05:31.600 --> 05:34.230
We weren't <i>that friendly,</i>

05:34.230 --> 05:37.560
since she left the orphanage as soon as she was adopted.

05:38.310 --> 05:41.570
Well, getting to the main point here...

05:41.570 --> 05:44.860
Do you mind telling Hirono-san

05:44.860 --> 05:47.530
not to strip naked in the Art Club Room?

05:48.280 --> 05:52.080
All the complaints come to me, you know.

05:52.080 --> 05:56.660
I just thought she might listen if <i>you told her.</i>

05:57.160 --> 05:58.540
Excuse me.

05:58.540 --> 05:59.080
Huh?

05:59.080 --> 06:00.750
W-Wait, Himura-kun!

06:13.970 --> 06:16.560
So this place is exactly like the ones in Japan.

06:18.980 --> 06:21.770
You'll get scolded for sitting in a place like that.

06:21.770 --> 06:22.770
By whom?

06:22.770 --> 06:24.980
Hmm... God?

06:24.980 --> 06:26.990
Nothing like that exists in this world.

06:26.990 --> 06:29.780
Well then, why are you in a church?

06:29.780 --> 06:32.070
A lot goes on in an adult's world.

06:32.830 --> 06:36.120
You make it sound like nothing goes on in a child's world.

06:36.620 --> 06:38.000
You might be right.

06:38.000 --> 06:41.500
Now that I think about it, a child's world might have a lot more going on.

06:41.500 --> 06:43.090
Don't you remember?

06:43.090 --> 06:44.090
I can't say.

06:44.090 --> 06:45.380
I've forgotten.

06:45.380 --> 06:49.800
Furthermore, an adult is just a child who's grown up.

06:50.800 --> 06:53.300
Are you Renji's cousin?

06:53.300 --> 06:54.510
How did you...

06:54.510 --> 06:58.020
I tend to know most things about this town.

06:58.020 --> 06:59.850
Is that true?

06:59.850 --> 07:00.940
I guess so.

07:02.270 --> 07:05.860
Well then, do you know about a musician, Kuze Shuichi-san?

07:06.860 --> 07:07.820
Yeah.

07:07.820 --> 07:10.110
Really? Perfect timing!

07:10.110 --> 07:13.820
Kuze-san and I were planning on hanging out today,

07:13.820 --> 07:17.040
but he must've gone somewhere, because he's not at home.

07:17.040 --> 07:19.330
I'm looking for him. Do you have any clues?

07:19.330 --> 07:21.830
It's not like I monitor Kuze or anything.

07:21.830 --> 07:25.130
But you just said that you know everything!

07:25.130 --> 07:27.000
I'll give you a warning.

07:28.170 --> 07:29.670
Don't associate with him.

07:30.550 --> 07:32.890
If you're going to delve deeply, be prepared.

07:39.350 --> 07:40.810
Hey, Kuze.

07:40.810 --> 07:43.480
You know a lot of girls at this school, don't you?

07:43.480 --> 07:45.020
That's rude.

07:45.020 --> 07:48.110
I also know a lot of girls that don't go to this school.

07:48.110 --> 07:50.280
Do you know anyone among the first years?

07:50.280 --> 07:52.660
Hopefully someone that can keep a secret.

07:52.660 --> 07:56.030
Doing you a favor before you go study abroad seems like a reasonable idea.

07:56.030 --> 07:58.870
You mean repaying a debt, don't you?

07:58.870 --> 08:01.000
What's up? Found yourself in a crisis?

08:02.250 --> 08:04.120
Something's been bugging me.

08:04.120 --> 08:06.380
So what sinister plot are you hatching now?

08:07.340 --> 08:08.670
Nagi!

08:08.670 --> 08:09.880
Why are you here?

08:09.880 --> 08:15.220
From the Art Room, I saw you two having an urgent conversation and trying to stay out of sight.

08:15.220 --> 08:17.100
You're making us sound bad.

08:17.100 --> 08:19.930
We were just confirming our friendship, that's all.

08:19.930 --> 08:20.930
Right?

08:20.930 --> 08:24.190
Well then, let me in on that friendship as well.

08:24.190 --> 08:25.560
It's okay.

08:25.560 --> 08:28.320
I'm not trying to brag or anything, but I can keep a secret.

08:28.320 --> 08:32.650
Well in your case, you don't have any friends to gossip with, right?

08:35.360 --> 08:37.700
Sorry, my bad.

08:37.990 --> 08:38.950
Forgiven.

08:38.950 --> 08:41.660
You always forgive people as soon as they apologize, don't you?

08:41.660 --> 08:45.000
I don't like dwelling on troubling emotions.

08:47.500 --> 08:52.090
So basically, all I have to do is ask around Yuko-chan's classroom?

08:52.090 --> 08:53.760
Please do it without being noticed.

08:53.760 --> 08:54.760
Roger.

08:54.760 --> 08:58.010
I don't like to see a pretty girl be sad, either.

09:01.970 --> 09:03.350
What's wrong, Nagi?

09:03.350 --> 09:04.100
Hey.

09:04.100 --> 09:05.020
Wait, Nagi!

09:05.020 --> 09:06.520
Where are you going? Hey!

09:06.520 --> 09:08.520
Serendipity

09:08.810 --> 09:10.020
What happened, Nagi?

09:10.020 --> 09:11.070
That.

09:12.940 --> 09:14.950
Yu, piggyback.

09:14.950 --> 09:15.650
Right...

09:17.700 --> 09:20.410
Could you lean to the right a little more?

09:22.620 --> 09:25.460
Hey Nagi, why are you barefoot too?

09:25.460 --> 09:29.380
Isn't that obvious? It's because I was drawing a rough draft just now, of course.

09:30.380 --> 09:32.250
You came here without even putting on your slippers?

09:32.250 --> 09:33.170
Yeah.

09:33.170 --> 09:36.010
I was in a hurry, so I just put on this white coat.

09:38.010 --> 09:39.050
Get off!

09:39.050 --> 09:40.470
Get off, right this second!

09:40.470 --> 09:41.720
Don't shake, Yu!

09:41.720 --> 09:43.390
I almost have them.

09:43.390 --> 09:44.520
Whoa!

09:45.480 --> 09:47.310
These are probably Yuko-chan's.

09:47.310 --> 09:50.270
You should say it like Yüko-chan, not Yuko-chan.

09:50.270 --> 09:53.230
A name longer than two syllables is too hard to say.

09:53.230 --> 09:55.650
How did you know they were up there?

09:55.650 --> 09:59.870
I've also lost my slippers in the past.

10:00.240 --> 10:01.490
I see.

10:01.490 --> 10:03.240
I can only say one thing.

10:03.410 --> 10:08.250
No one would hide slippers up there without malicious intent.

10:08.250 --> 10:10.630
And I can only say one thing.

10:10.630 --> 10:14.210
Hurry up and take those slippers to her.

10:15.010 --> 10:18.510
A shard of the dream falls from my hand

10:15.010 --> 10:18.510
In order to find the lost answer, I start to run

10:38.200 --> 10:41.200
Trains... don't stop at this station.

10:41.200 --> 10:43.620
U-Um... Long time no see!

10:43.620 --> 10:44.540
Huh?

10:44.540 --> 10:46.870
You're Chihiro-senpai, right?

10:46.870 --> 10:49.750
Yes. My name is Shindou Chihiro.

10:49.750 --> 10:52.380
Um, I'm Hayama Mizuki!

10:52.380 --> 10:55.630
I played with you and Kei-senpai when we were small,

10:55.630 --> 10:57.880
and we've definitely met before...

10:57.880 --> 10:59.220
Don't you remember?

11:00.380 --> 11:01.640
Mizuki-chan?

11:01.640 --> 11:04.140
Yes! I'm Mizuki-chan!

11:04.140 --> 11:06.640
You've grown so much!

11:06.640 --> 11:07.430
Huh?

11:07.430 --> 11:08.560
Oh.

11:08.560 --> 11:12.650
Yes, well, my body just grew on its own.

11:12.650 --> 11:16.070
I see. A lot of time has passed.

11:16.070 --> 11:19.440
Chihiro-senpai, you've grown too.

11:19.440 --> 11:21.240
You're so pretty!

11:21.240 --> 11:25.080
It's a mysterious kind of charm compared to Kei-senpai's, and it's dazzling!

11:25.080 --> 11:26.290
"Dazzling"?

11:26.290 --> 11:28.290
In other words, you're beautiful!

11:28.290 --> 11:30.540
Th-That's not true.

11:30.540 --> 11:32.960
Oh, but it is!

11:32.960 --> 11:34.330
And having said that,

11:34.330 --> 11:36.300
may I hug you?

11:36.300 --> 11:36.920
Huh?

11:36.920 --> 11:39.880
A hug, to celebrate our reunion?

11:39.880 --> 11:40.670
Y-Yes.

11:40.670 --> 11:42.180
Yay!

11:43.090 --> 11:45.550
So soft...

11:45.550 --> 11:47.180
Smells so good.

11:48.180 --> 11:51.640
My senpai energies are being recharged.

11:51.640 --> 11:53.350
Ah, I'm happy.

11:53.350 --> 11:54.690
Ugh.

11:54.690 --> 11:56.980
This isn't good. I'm about to have a nosebleed.

12:01.280 --> 12:03.950
He took Chihiro-senpai?

12:03.950 --> 12:06.030
That Renji, how dare he!

12:06.030 --> 12:08.040
You're too good for him!

12:08.040 --> 12:13.500
No, I'm the one who's always causing trouble for Renji-kun.

12:14.170 --> 12:15.750
I'm a little disappointed.

12:15.750 --> 12:20.090
When I think about how Kei-senpai and Chihiro-senpai have found someone sweet,

12:20.300 --> 12:23.840
it feels like my sense of heartbreak has doubled or tripled in size.

12:25.090 --> 12:28.930
Oh, we won't get into whether Renji is sweet or not.

12:28.930 --> 12:31.770
Mizuki-chan, you've experienced heartbreak?

12:31.770 --> 12:32.890
Huh?

12:32.890 --> 12:36.060
Oh, no! It's not anything that major!

12:36.060 --> 12:39.440
I just couldn't see someone that I really wanted to see.

12:39.440 --> 12:40.650
I understand.

12:40.650 --> 12:45.160
When I can't see someone I want to see, I feel like my chest is being squeezed.

12:45.160 --> 12:48.030
Even if it's just for a little while...

12:49.660 --> 12:52.910
I wonder where Kuze-san went?

12:53.210 --> 12:55.580
Maybe he's avoiding me.

12:55.580 --> 12:56.250
Huh?

12:57.290 --> 12:59.710
Maybe I took things a little too quickly.

12:59.710 --> 13:01.300
I might have done myself in.

13:02.090 --> 13:04.010
One second, please.

13:04.010 --> 13:06.930
Is that your diary, Chihiro-senpai?

13:06.930 --> 13:10.890
Yes. I always write down the most important things in here.

13:10.890 --> 13:12.640
If I remember correctly, Kuze-san is...

13:13.770 --> 13:15.020
Ah, there it is.

13:16.520 --> 13:19.560
Just as I thought. So that's how it is, huh?

13:19.560 --> 13:20.860
What's wrong?

13:20.860 --> 13:23.440
Oh! Um...

13:23.440 --> 13:25.030
Nothing!

13:25.030 --> 13:28.740
From your reaction, it most certainly is <i>not "nothing!"</i>

13:28.740 --> 13:29.660
Huh?

13:29.660 --> 13:31.660
Is it a secret? Is it private?

13:31.660 --> 13:32.700
Is it confidential information?

13:32.700 --> 13:35.120
Is it something you guys are hiding from me?

13:35.120 --> 13:37.330
No, it's nothing like that.

13:37.330 --> 13:39.040
Well then, what is it?

13:39.040 --> 13:40.210
Well...

13:40.210 --> 13:43.210
Mizuki-chan, do you love Kuze-san?

13:43.210 --> 13:43.800
Huh?

13:43.800 --> 13:45.170
Well, um...

13:45.170 --> 13:48.220
If you ask me so directly...

13:48.220 --> 13:53.060
Apparently, coming to love someone means that there's nothing you can do about it.

13:54.180 --> 13:57.520
Mizuki-chan, is that how you feel?

14:01.520 --> 14:07.110
I'm not quite there yet, but I'm scared that I will be soon.

14:09.990 --> 14:11.740
I see.

14:11.740 --> 14:14.120
Then I guess it can't be helped.

14:14.910 --> 14:16.870
It's about Kuze-san.

14:24.050 --> 14:26.380
You look terrible, Kuze.

14:26.380 --> 14:28.880
Yeah, I've been better.

14:28.880 --> 14:30.720
She came by earlier.

14:30.720 --> 14:32.220
She was looking for you.

14:32.220 --> 14:33.930
I see.

14:33.930 --> 14:36.430
Is that why you're looking like this?

14:36.430 --> 14:38.890
You understand, don't you, Himura?

14:38.890 --> 14:43.270
Even if it's just a joke, I can't have a girl say that she loves me.

14:43.270 --> 14:44.820
She said that?

14:44.820 --> 14:47.400
Because of it, my dreams have become horrendous.

14:48.900 --> 14:50.780
I'll settle it tonight.

14:50.780 --> 14:51.660
Are you going to do it?

14:51.660 --> 14:52.820
Yeah.

14:52.820 --> 14:54.700
This is the last of my regrets.

14:54.700 --> 14:55.830
I see.

14:55.830 --> 14:57.620
I have to bury it.

14:57.620 --> 14:59.500
Everything. Thoroughly.

14:59.500 --> 15:01.920
I have to clear everything...

15:02.460 --> 15:04.920
since I'm going to die.

15:04.920 --> 15:06.460
Later.

15:08.260 --> 15:10.220
Gute Reise, Kuze.

15:08.260 --> 15:10.220
Gute Reise is German for "Have a good trip!"

15:10.470 --> 15:11.970
Life

15:11.970 --> 15:13.600
This means...

15:14.050 --> 15:17.100
Kuze-san... is going to die?

15:17.100 --> 15:20.100
I heard he has a rare type of cardiomyopathy.

15:21.100 --> 15:22.940
Renji.

15:22.940 --> 15:27.650
Six months ago, he collapsed from a heart attack during a concert.

15:27.650 --> 15:30.150
Apparently, there's nothing else they can do.

15:30.150 --> 15:32.450
Is that... true?

15:32.450 --> 15:35.120
Yes. He said that nothing can be done.

15:35.120 --> 15:37.160
He doesn't want people to fuss or worry about him.

15:37.160 --> 15:40.250
He wants everyone to act naturally, like they always have.

15:40.250 --> 15:43.460
That's what Kuze-san specifically asked us to do.

15:43.460 --> 15:45.340
Kuze-san...

15:45.340 --> 15:48.170
He's been spending time with me, even in his condition.

15:48.170 --> 15:49.460
Despite that, I...

15:49.460 --> 15:53.720
No, he'd prefer that you not take his situation into consideration.

15:53.720 --> 15:54.470
But!

16:00.520 --> 16:05.310
Mizuki-chan, many people have that kind of resolve.

16:05.310 --> 16:08.020
It's just one way of living.

16:11.530 --> 16:13.030
You

16:15.570 --> 16:18.910
Oh? What's up, Himura-senpai?

16:18.910 --> 16:20.910
What are you doing here all alone?

16:22.540 --> 16:23.540
Here.

16:23.540 --> 16:26.080
You went to the trouble of finding them for me?

16:26.080 --> 16:27.920
I found them... by coincidence.

16:27.920 --> 16:29.500
Thank you very much!

16:31.050 --> 16:32.470
It fits perfectly.

16:32.470 --> 16:35.220
Now I can marry Prince Charming, right?

16:36.470 --> 16:38.720
Oh, you were staying after school?

16:38.720 --> 16:39.970
IDIOT

16:38.720 --> 16:39.970
DIE

16:38.720 --> 16:39.970
UGLY

16:38.720 --> 16:39.970
YOU'RE SO

16:38.720 --> 16:39.970
ANNOYING

16:39.970 --> 16:40.970
Hey.

16:40.970 --> 16:42.600
It's pretty interesting, isn't it?

16:42.600 --> 16:44.020
Those bastards...

16:44.020 --> 16:45.850
You've gotten quite a foul mouth.

16:45.850 --> 16:48.320
Why are you so calm?

16:48.320 --> 16:51.320
Why are <i>you mad, Himura-senpai?</i>

16:51.320 --> 16:52.490
Huh?

16:52.490 --> 16:55.160
Is it because you love me, perhaps?

16:55.160 --> 16:58.030
I'm not in the mood for your jokes.

16:58.030 --> 17:00.950
I'm not the least bit bothered by it, which is why I can make jokes.

17:00.950 --> 17:04.120
For me, this is just an everyday event.

17:04.120 --> 17:05.710
An everyday event?

17:05.710 --> 17:07.790
It's not that hard.

17:07.790 --> 17:10.170
If I were to grade it, it would be "medium bullying".

17:10.170 --> 17:12.840
There's no "medium" or "well-done" in bullying!

17:12.840 --> 17:16.260
Well, those girls are at an age when they also have their own problems.

17:16.260 --> 17:19.390
Perhaps they need a way to relieve their stress?

17:19.390 --> 17:26.520
I guess an isolated, frail girl like me seems to make a perfect target.

17:32.110 --> 17:34.860
It's... not going to work anymore.

17:35.150 --> 17:36.400
Liar.

17:36.400 --> 17:37.780
Mizuki-chan?

17:40.580 --> 17:42.620
Chihiro-senpai?

17:42.620 --> 17:45.000
A message from Himura-san.

17:45.000 --> 17:47.210
Himura-san... from that church?

17:47.210 --> 17:52.460
He said that if you want to hear Kuze-san's violin, you ought to go to the beach tonight.

17:53.420 --> 17:58.090
Apparently, it's his policy not to interfere,

17:58.090 --> 18:01.100
but he said that he should at least tell <i>you.</i>

18:02.350 --> 18:06.140
He also mentioned that this might be the last chance.

18:09.560 --> 18:10.810
Kuze-san!

19:26.140 --> 19:27.720
I'm so pathetic.

19:40.240 --> 19:41.490
Mizuki-chan?

19:44.530 --> 19:45.910
Mizuki-chan!

19:45.910 --> 19:47.490
Stop it! It's useless!

20:00.470 --> 20:01.970
Mizuki-chan!

20:08.390 --> 20:10.430
I did it, Kuze-san!

20:12.480 --> 20:13.900
Let me see your hands.

20:15.400 --> 20:16.610
Show me your hands!

20:22.860 --> 20:24.070
You idiot!

20:26.450 --> 20:28.580
I'm sorry.

20:28.580 --> 20:29.910
I...

20:29.910 --> 20:34.080
You... can't do that yet.

20:34.080 --> 20:37.340
Because... you're still alive.

20:39.210 --> 20:40.800
Please...

20:42.300 --> 20:44.380
It's all right.

20:44.380 --> 20:45.890
It's going to be okay.

21:01.490 --> 21:14.870
The shining wind calmly sways from gaps in the clouds.

21:15.460 --> 21:22.300
The echoing sounds sparkle.

21:22.420 --> 21:25.800
Even if it's a hope that was nearly lost,

21:26.050 --> 21:33.430
I should be able to find it again

21:35.730 --> 21:38.610
Holding firmly onto your sound,

21:39.230 --> 21:48.780
I don't let go of your hand joined with mine.

21:49.740 --> 21:55.580
Please don't forget the important things.

21:56.750 --> 22:03.260
A smile continues on into the future.

22:17.020 --> 22:19.770
also

22:17.600 --> 22:20.770
I guess being bullied isn't always so bad.

22:20.770 --> 22:21.900
What do you mean?

22:21.900 --> 22:24.980
Well, you're going to walk me home,

22:24.980 --> 22:27.780
even though you told me not to come near you.

22:27.780 --> 22:29.780
I just remembered. Don't come near me.

22:29.780 --> 22:31.240
Eh?

22:31.240 --> 22:33.080
Just joking. Let's go.

22:33.080 --> 22:34.080
Geez.

22:36.700 --> 22:38.210
What's wrong, Yuko?

22:38.210 --> 22:39.500
What are you doing?

22:39.500 --> 22:43.170
I seem to have really bad luck with shoes.

22:46.880 --> 22:48.220
We're going.

22:48.220 --> 22:49.590
Where?

22:49.590 --> 22:54.140
You said something about them being stressed out earlier, right?

22:54.140 --> 22:57.020
You know who the culprits are, don't you?

22:57.020 --> 23:00.230
I should really watch what I say in front of you, senpai.

23:00.230 --> 23:03.110
Let's leave them alone. It's not a big deal.

23:03.110 --> 23:04.400
Yes it is!

23:04.400 --> 23:05.610
This is too cruel!

23:05.610 --> 23:08.240
It's not something that <i>you should be mad about, senpai.</i>

23:08.240 --> 23:10.530
Why do you care so much?

23:10.530 --> 23:12.280
Because it's such a cheap trick!

23:12.280 --> 23:14.740
I consider this level of pranks to be cute.

23:14.740 --> 23:16.370
"This level"?

23:16.370 --> 23:18.410
What standards are you using?

23:18.410 --> 23:19.370
That's because...

23:21.000 --> 23:25.000
Isn't that part of human nature?

23:25.840 --> 23:27.960
The feelings that have been incised.

23:27.960 --> 23:31.050
The sins that will never disappear.

23:31.050 --> 23:34.350
ef - a tale of melodies.

23:34.350 --> 23:35.510
Turn.

23:35.680 --> 23:39.980
Can you hear it? The melody of truth.
